<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3677" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">armentārĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>pertaining to a herd of cattle</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">morbi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sol. 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">equiso,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 7</span></i>
			.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">armentārĭus</span></b> , ii,
				m.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A herdsman</i>, <i>neat-herd</i>,
			* <i><span class="en">Lucr. 6, 1252</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 2, 5, 18</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnia secum Armentarius Afer agit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 3, 344</span></i>
			: armentarius ego sum, * <i><span class="en">Vulg.
				Amos, 7, 14</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A surname of the emperor Galerius Maximianus</i>,
				<i>whose ancestors were shepherds</i>, <i><span class="en">Aur. Vict.
				Ep. 40</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
